    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What sets General Motors apart from other automakers?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "General Motors (GM) sets itself apart with deep design and engineering expertise, iconic brands, and a clear vision for the future. For over a century, we’ve built vehicles that people trust. Today, we continue to push the industry forward, creating the one for every drive and leading the way toward a world with zero crashes, zero emissions, and zero congestion."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is GM the largest automaker in the U.S.?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, GM led the US. automotive industry in total, retail, and fleet sales for the first quarter of 2025, with 17% market share across its brands."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does General Motors stand for?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "At General Motors, we’re driven by a passion to create the one for every purpose and journey. Since 1908, we’ve been continually advancing the automotive industry, raising the bar for excellence with every innovation and moving people forward. Today, we’re working toward a future with zero crashes, zero emissions, and zero congestion—for every driver, every purpose, and every road ahead."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are GM cars reliable?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "GM vehicles are well-known for their long-lasting reliability, strong safety standards, and consistent performance. Since 1908, GM has prioritized excellence, reliability, and safety through rigorous testing and innovative engineering."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How is GM making vehicle technology more innovative?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "GM’s Research and Development team drives innovation for GM customers. Specifically, the team works on advancing battery materials and systems, energy and propulsion systems, materials and manufacturing, connected vehicle tech, and software-defined technology. These innovations help create smarter, more efficient, and future-ready vehicles."
      }
    }
  ]
}


{
"@context": "https://schema.org/",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What makes General Motors design and engineering special?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "At GM, we thrive at the intersection of design and engineering, creating simplicity from complexity to make vehicles that customers are proud to own and love to drive. From becoming the first automotive manufacturer to standardize the automotive design process in product development to introducing innovations like Super Cruise hands-free driver assistance technology and Google Built-in, we’ve always designed our vehicles with technical expertise to make driving smarter, safer, and more enjoyable."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is GM's engineering and design process?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "GM’s design and engineering teams work together to blend creativity with technology. Concepts are developed, tested, and refined before being brought to life by manufacturing teams in state-of-the-art facilities."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does GM make autonomous vehicles?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "GM offers advanced driver assistance systems (ADAS) like Super Cruise, which provide hands-free driver assistance on compatible roads but still require the driver to stay attentive. Super Cruise is powered by a Unified Lateral Controller — a self-learning, modular software system that uses real-time data and machine learning to manage lane centering, smooth lane changes, and adaptive steering."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How has General Motors shaped the history of automotive engineering?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "For over a century, General Motors (GM) has been at the forefront of automotive engineering. From introducing the first mass-produced turbocharged car to pioneering the modern electric vehicle, electric pickup, and in-car touchscreen, GM has consistently led with bold ideas and real impact. We engineer the one for every drive and will continue to drive automotive innovation for generations to come. It’s part of our DNA."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are GM's design and engineering facilities like?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "GM’s new Design West facility, along with its predecessor, the Saarinen Building, are testaments to the creative forces that have defined GM’s design ethos since its founding. Design West’s large, open spaces allow for teams to congregate around the design process."
      }
    }
  ]
}


{
